{"nodes": [{"id": "phase3doc_r3f_migration", "label": "Phase 3 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d React Three Fiber Migration Plan", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "phase3doc_gamecontroller", "label": "GameController (imperative three.js)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "~1000 lines of imperative three.js construction tightly bound to a single requestAnimationFrame loop driving both rendering and cannon physics. Identified as the primary migration target because component reuse is hard, hot-reload is impossible, testing is painful, and onboarding is slow."}, {"id": "phase3doc_r3f", "label": "React Three Fiber (R3F)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen over imperative three.js for declarative scene description, Suspense for asset loading, and a community ecosystem (@react-three/cannon, @react-three/drei, @react-three/postprocessing)."}, {"id": "phase3doc_scenedsl", "label": "src/r3f/sceneDSL.js \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Scene DSL", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 67", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Declarative scene-description format that builds vanilla three.js objects today and maps 1:1 onto R3F JSX. Enables bottle/block/particle entities to be expressed as ~30 lines of data instead of ~150 lines of imperative ceremony, making entities testable and R3F-ready without requiring the full stack upgrade."}, {"id": "phase3doc_bottlecapstack", "label": "src/r3f/bottleCapStack.js \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Bottle Cap Stack", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 69", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "phase3doc_r3fadapter", "label": "src/r3f/r3fAdapter.js \u00e2\u20ac\u201d R3F Adapter", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "phase3doc_subphase3a", "label": "Sub-phase 3a \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Foundation (Shipped)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 62", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "phase3doc_subphase3b", "label": "Sub-phase 3b \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Stack Upgrade", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 91", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "phase3doc_subphase3c", "label": "Sub-phase 3c \u00e2\u20ac\u201d R3F Install + Decomposition", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 116", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "phase3doc_subphase3d", "label": "Sub-phase 3d \u00e2\u20ac\u201d RAF/Physics Coupling Rework", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 135", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "phase3doc_cameracontroller", "label": "CameraController (State Machine Rewrite)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 219", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Complete rewrite of CameraController.js as a state machine driven by user spec: front-facing label always centered, shoulder pitch, random projection swap, three random mid-flip modes, failed-state grading. Label tracking uses block-travel axis (not bottle label normal) to avoid clipping into restaurant walls, with bottle inner-mesh yaw forcibly overridden each frame via setLabelFaceDirection."}, {"id": "phase3doc_label_tracking", "label": "Label Tracking Design \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Block-Travel Axis Strategy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 259", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Camera position uses the block-travel axis (current\u00e2\u2020\u2019next block, ground-projected) not the bottle's actual label normal. This guarantees a clean sightline along the gameplay path without ever clipping into props. Bottle inner-mesh yaw is forcibly rotated each frame so the label always faces the camera; override suspended during FLIP state so the bottle can spin freely mid-air."}, {"id": "phase3doc_flip_modes", "label": "Three Flip Camera Modes (FOLLOW/LOCKED/CINEMATIC_CUT)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 280", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Random mid-flip behaviour selected by injected RNG: FOLLOW tracks bottle in flight, LOCKED snapshots pose allowing off-frame travel, CINEMATIC_CUT hard-cuts to perpendicular side-on pose. RNG-injectable for deterministic test coverage."}, {"id": "phase3doc_projection_swap", "label": "Random Projection Swap (Ortho/Persp) on Landing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 296", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each LANDING transition coin-flips between OrthographicCamera and PerspectiveCamera. Pose is carried over to the new active camera so the swap is invisible until the next breathing/lerp tick. Both cameras share fade overlay (each parented to one) so failed-state grading works regardless of active projection."}, {"id": "phase3doc_worldscene", "label": "WorldScene.js Changes", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 326", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "phase3doc_bottlejs", "label": "Bottle.js Entity", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 324", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "phase3doc_cannon_physics", "label": "Cannon Physics Integration", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 130", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Identified as highest-risk R3F migration item. Currently hand-rolled world.step()+body sync; target is @react-three/cannon <Physics>. Tween+physics+game-state machine are tightly interleaved; deterministic event log in gameStore + replay test are the mitigation strategy."}, {"id": "phase3doc_tweenjs", "label": "@tweenjs/tween.js", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 338", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unmaintained. R3F community uses framer-motion-3d or motion-three. Migration of every tween call site is a separate week of work that can happen in parallel with sub-phase 3c."}], "edges": [{"source": "phase3doc_r3f_migration", "target": "phase3doc_gamecontroller", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 17", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "phase3doc_r3f_migration", "target": "phase3doc_r3f", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 19", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "phase3doc_r3f_migration", "target": "phase3doc_subphase3a", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 62", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "phase3doc_r3f_migration", "target": "phase3doc_subphase3b", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 91", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "phase3doc_r3f_migration", "target": "phase3doc_subphase3c", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 116", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "phase3doc_r3f_migration", "target": "phase3doc_subphase3d", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 135", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "phase3doc_subphase3a", "target": "phase3doc_scenedsl", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 67", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "phase3doc_subphase3a", "target": "phase3doc_bottlecapstack", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 69", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "phase3doc_subphase3a", "target": "phase3doc_r3fadapter", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migration.md", "source_location": "line 71", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "phase3doc_subphase3b", "target": "phase3doc_subphase3a", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/phase-3-r3f-migratio